# Otto Kernel

Kernel lives in unified ROM build with P-Machine (0x0000–0x5FFF). RAM map: `kernel/memmap.asm`.

## After every kernel change

```bash
source .venv/bin/activate && ./generate-all.sh
```

Regenerates ROMs, **symbols.asm**, and all apps. Never hand-edit `kernel/symbols.asm`.

After flashing EEPROMs, snapshot symbols for hardware targets:

```bash
./scripts/save-kernel-abi.sh              # or ./generate-all.sh --save-abi
./scripts/build-apps.sh --abi v1.2.101    # apps for older kernel on hardware
```

Snapshots live in `kernel/abi/v<version>/`. Helpers in `scripts/lib/kernel-abi.sh`. See `kernel/abi/README.md`.

## Interrupt handlers (pointers in kernel RAM)

| Source | Pointer addr |
|--------|----------------|
| INT1 | 0x83F8–0x83F9 |
| INT2 (serial) | 0x83FA–0x83FB |
| TIMER (10 Hz) | 0x83FC–0x83FD |
| KEYBOARD | 0x83FE–0x83FF |

Mask bits: EXT1=0x01, EXT2=0x02, TIMER=0x04, KEYBOARD=0x08. Setup: write handler MSB/LSB, `TIA`/`ORA`/`TAI`, `CLI`.

## Key kernel API (call via `JSR`, include `symbols.asm`)

**Serial**: `ACIA_INIT`, `ACIA_SEND_CHAR` (A), `ACIA_SEND_STRING` (D:E), `ACIA_READ_CHAR`, `ACIA_PULL_FROM_BUFFER`

**VT100**: `VT100_ERASE_SCREEN`, `VT100_CURSOR_POSITION` (D=row, E=col), `VT100_TEXT_RESET`

**Math**: `MULTIPLY_INT`, `DIVIDE_INT`, `MUL16S`, `DIV16S`, `MOD16S`, `CMP16S` (use `MATH16_A`/`MATH16_B`)

**Transfer**: `XMODEM_RCV`

Full symbol table and addresses: `kernel/symbols.asm` and `AGENTS.md`.
